# Implementation Plan: UI/UX Fixes & Demo Prep

This plan addresses the bugs and UX friction points you identified during your testing, specifically targeting the 500 error on the Admin cycle toggle, simplifying the Admin workflows, replacing raw JSON with polished UI dashboards, and making the goal setting process easier to demonstrate.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]  
> **Auth Constraint (Create Users)**
> You requested that admins can create new users and assign temporary passwords. Because this project uses **Supabase** for authentication, creating an authenticated user with a password requires the `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, which is not safely exposed to the frontend and typically isn't configured in the backend `.env` for this repo.
> 
> **Proposed Solution**: I will build the "Create User" UI in `app.admin.users.tsx` and a backend endpoint `POST /api/v1/users/demo-create` that writes the user directly to the PostgreSQL `users` table so they appear in the system hierarchy for your demo. However, they **will not be able to actually log in** unless you separately create them in the Supabase Dashboard. If this is purely for demonstrating the hierarchy feature, this should suffice.

